       "text": "# No\n\nUnder the Consumer Insurance (Disclosure and Representations) Act 2012 (the standard applicable to residential buildings insurance), a policyholder must disclose facts they know, or ought to know, are material to the insurance decision. The fact that the building stands empty for extended periods in winter—increasing the risk of pipe damage—is material information that Sutton ought to have disclosed, regardless of whether the form asked about it. By failing to disclose this material fact, the standard was not met, and the insurer could refuse the claim.",
